    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns a formidable 81.88 score against Grant Holmes. **Henderson**\u2019s massive projection is bolstered by an elite 18% SP skill advantage and a park factor that suggests a massive power breakout. Following closely, **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci** provide high-floor stability atop their respective lineups; **Antonacci**\u2019s 67.67 score is specifically driven by a favorable matchup against the hittable Spencer Arrighetti, combined with the optimizer\u2019s heavy weighting toward his speed profile in our 5x5 Roto context. **Heliot Ramos** also looks like a prime asset against Grayson Rodriguez, where a 5.27 xERA for the starter and a wind-out advantage elevate his efficiency score to 64.64.\n\nSeveral players carry significant situational edges today, most notably **Nasim Nunez**, whose 62.15 score is inflated by a rare 4% boost derived from Eduardo Rodriguez\u2019s notoriously slow delivery, creating a high-upside environment for stolen bases. Conversely, **Kyle Tucker** faces a tougher test against Sean Manaea; while his raw talent maintains a solid 57.25, the combination of a negative park factor and a lefty-on-lefty platoon disadvantage keeps him in the marginal range for today\u2019s start. The tightest bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas**, who landed at 60.53. Despite his favorable xwOBA and the same SB-friendly conditions facing **Nunez**, **Vargas** ultimately missed the cut as the optimizer favored the higher lineup placement and defensive stability of the starting infield. Owners should monitor all lineups closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board remains the primary risk factor; weather and late-scratch potential could shift these projections rapidly before first pitch.",
